{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform" or render_mode == "action" %}
{# The armed company at the player's back, shown to bystanders only: not to its own members
   (0187 gives them their camp's voice), the player, or the player's companions, who know who
   these fighters are. sever_war_band is the same player-state text for everyone; "" when none. #}
{% if actorUUID and actorUUID != 0 %}
{% set warband = sever_war_band(actorUUID) %}
{% if warband != "" %}
{% if sever_camp_mustered(actorUUID) != "1" and actorUUID != player.UUID and not is_follower(actorUUID) and is_sever_follower(actorUUID) == "" %}
## The Company {{ player.name }} Keeps
{{ warband }}
- You don't know who these fighters are or where they came from. All you have is what your eyes tell you: armed, easy about it, and following one person's lead.
- Let it weigh on you the way it would weigh on anyone. Most folk get careful around armed company — softer voice, fairer price, shorter argument. A guard stays civil but starts counting heads. Someone bold might still push their luck; they just know exactly what they are pushing against.
- Unless a fight is already on, nothing about them says rampage. It is the quiet kind of dangerous, and quiet is worse.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
